          <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-2xl text-gray-900">Anonymous reviews</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          When you choose to post a review anonymously, your name is hidden from the public version of the review. We retain your identity internally for moderation and abuse prevention, but we do not share it with the judge being reviewed, the court, or any third party except as required by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-2xl text-gray-900">What we do not do</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 pl-6 space-y-2 list-disc">
          <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
          <li>We do not share reviewer identities with judges or courts.</li>
          <li>We do not run third-party advertising on the site.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-2xl text-gray-900">Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We use first-party cookies for authentication and to remember your preferences.
          We do not currently set advertising or third-party tracking cookies, and we do
          not sell your data. If that changes, we will ask for your consent before setting
          any non-essential cookie. You can clear or block cookies in your browser at any
          time, though signing in will not work without the authentication cookie.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-2xl text-gray-900">How long we keep things</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <strong>Your account.</strong> We keep account data for as long as the account
          exists. When you delete your account we remove your profile, your reviews and
          comments, your drafts, your saved preferences and the notifications attached to
          them. Deletion is not reversible.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <strong>Anonymous reviews.</strong> Posting anonymously hides your name from the
          public review. We still hold the link between you and that review internally,
          because without it we cannot let you edit or delete your own review, and we
          cannot act on abuse. We keep that link for as long as the review is published.
          If you delete the review or your account, the link goes with it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <strong>Moderation records.</strong> When a moderator approves, declines or
          removes something, we keep a record of that decision — who made it, when, and
          what it concerned — for two years. We keep these even after the underlying
          content is gone, because they are how we answer a later complaint about how a
          decision was made.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <strong>Server and email logs.</strong> Operational logs are kept for 90 days.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
