        <p class="mt-4">
          We are sometimes asked — by a subpoena, court order or demand letter — to
          identify the person behind an anonymous review. We do not hand over a reviewer's
          identity in response to a demand letter alone. Where we receive legal process,
          we review it for validity and scope, and where the law allows it we notify the
          affected user first and give them a reasonable opportunity to object before we
          respond, unless we are legally prohibited from telling them.
        </p>
